# SIA model routing (optional)
#
# SIA's router decides per-request whether to use the local MLX model or
# the remote Groq API. Most of the routing logic is automatic — the
# heuristic / classifier work without configuration. This file exists
# for the cases where you want to nudge specific call sites toward a
# specific provider/model.
#
# Status: currently *advisory*. The serving API consults the env vars
# below directly; this YAML file is documented here so the convention
# stays consistent with multi_agent_planner's config/model_routing.yml,
# which uses the same shape. If/when SIA grows a per-role inference
# split (e.g. "evaluation should use Groq even when chat uses local"),
# this file will become load-bearing.
#
# Environment variables that ARE currently load-bearing:
#
#   SIA_ROUTING_MODE     auto | local-only | remote-only
#                        (default: auto)
#
#   COMPLEXITY_THRESHOLD float 0-1 (default 0.5)
#                        Heuristic score at-or-above this routes remote.
#
#   SIA_CLASSIFIER_PATH  path/to/clf.json (default models/complexity_classifier.json)
#                        Lazy-loaded classifier weights; overrides the heuristic
#                        when its confidence is high enough.
#
#   GROQ_MODEL           Groq model id (default: llama-3.3-70b-versatile)
#   MLX_MODEL            HF id of the local MLX model
#                        (default: mlx-community/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct-4bit)
#
# Future per-role routing (parsed by core.providers.router when wired in):
#
# chat:        mlx/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct-4bit
# evaluation:  groq/llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# distillation: groq/llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# judging:     groq/llama-3.3-70b-versatile
